## Five things we learned running on-call for a year.
Swipe →

---
intent: problem
eyebrow: 01
notes: The starting point: nobody knew who was on call.
---
## Nobody knew who was on call.

::: metrics
- 40 min | to find the right person | Measured on the twelve incidents of the first quarter. {.hero}
:::

---
intent: explain
eyebrow: 02
notes: What changed, in three steps.
---
## We put the rota next to the runbooks.

::: timeline
- Week 1 | The rota moved out of the spreadsheet.
- Week 2 | Every runbook got an owner and a last-reviewed date.
- Week 3 | Handover notes at every shift change.
:::

---
intent: reveal
eyebrow: 03
notes: The one number.
---
## Time to the right person, a year later.

::: metrics
- 40 min | before
- 4 min | after {.hero}
:::

---
intent: decide
eyebrow: 04
notes: The trade-off we made.
---
## A rota you edit, or a rota that edits you?

::: compare
### The spreadsheet
- Free and familiar.
- Out of date the day after.

### The tool {.hero}
- The rota, the runbooks and the requests are one thing.
- The manager reads the week instead of asking about it.
:::

